WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.320
Breaking news, everyone. The United

00:00:01.920 --> 00:00:07.560
States government has just given debt

00:00:04.320 --> 00:00:10.480
collectors more power. Two major changes

00:00:07.560 --> 00:00:13.960
just happened on how medical debt is

00:00:10.480 --> 00:00:17.000
[music] collected and how it can impact

00:00:13.960 --> 00:00:17.680
your credit reports and credit scores

00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:20.440
after [music]

00:00:17.680 --> 00:00:21.880
July 1st, 2026.

00:00:20.440 --> 00:00:25.120
And in this video, I'm going to break

00:00:21.880 --> 00:00:27.160
down these two changes and the steps you

00:00:25.120 --> 00:00:30.240
need to take right now to protect

00:00:27.160 --> 00:00:32.680
yourself if you receive a medical

00:00:30.240 --> 00:00:36.000
collection. The first major change,

00:00:32.680 --> 00:00:38.520
Senate Republicans block restoration of

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:40.560
medical debt protections. Now, here's

00:00:38.520 --> 00:00:43.120
what happened. Democrats tried to use

00:00:40.560 --> 00:00:45.960
the Congressional Review Act to overturn

00:00:43.120 --> 00:00:49.280
the Trump administration rollback of the

00:00:45.960 --> 00:00:51.760
Biden protection when it came to medical

00:00:49.280 --> 00:00:54.000
debt collections. Now, that rule was

00:00:51.760 --> 00:00:57.040
designed to give consumers additional

00:00:54.000 --> 00:01:00.040
protection when it came down to medical

00:00:57.040 --> 00:01:02.520
debt collections. But, Republican

00:01:00.040 --> 00:01:05.400
senators blocked the rollback. And why

00:01:02.520 --> 00:01:07.880
this is important because with those

00:01:05.400 --> 00:01:10.480
protections, many Americans, when it

00:01:07.880 --> 00:01:13.040
comes down to medical debts, this is one

00:01:10.480 --> 00:01:15.560
of the largest impacts on people's

00:01:13.040 --> 00:01:18.320
credit scores. And unlike any other

00:01:15.560 --> 00:01:20.560
collection, if you get sick, you cannot

00:01:18.320 --> 00:01:24.560
control your loved one from getting

00:01:20.560 --> 00:01:27.680
cancer or you yourself or being able to

00:01:24.560 --> 00:01:30.640
pay back those types of collections when

00:01:27.680 --> 00:01:33.960
it comes down to high medical costs.

00:01:30.640 --> 00:01:37.000
This is a debt not of your own doing and

00:01:33.960 --> 00:01:40.120
one of the top reasons why Americans

00:01:37.000 --> 00:01:42.520
file for bankruptcy. Now, advocates of

00:01:40.120 --> 00:01:45.480
the protection will state that someone

00:01:42.520 --> 00:01:47.800
with medical debt does not reflect them

00:01:45.480 --> 00:01:50.880
paying their bills on time for getting

00:01:47.800 --> 00:01:54.400
sick over something they cannot control.

00:01:50.880 --> 00:01:57.320
But, Republican senators and others that

00:01:54.400 --> 00:02:01.520
agree with the rollback argue that this

00:01:57.320 --> 00:02:04.880
is fair for the finance and lending to

00:02:01.520 --> 00:02:08.240
be able to understand your full credit

00:02:04.880 --> 00:02:11.920
history and any outstanding debts. This

00:02:08.240 --> 00:02:15.560
plays a part of your ability to pay back

00:02:11.920 --> 00:02:16.920
the bank or any lending debt obligation.

00:02:15.560 --> 00:02:19.120
Now, give me your opinion. Do you

00:02:16.920 --> 00:02:21.920
believe that these protections for

00:02:19.120 --> 00:02:24.320
medical debts should be in place or do

00:02:21.920 --> 00:02:27.320
you believe that the rollback is

00:02:24.320 --> 00:02:30.200
necessary? And banks and lenders do need

00:02:27.320 --> 00:02:33.200
accurate information in order to judge

00:02:30.200 --> 00:02:35.280
your ability to repay back debts and

00:02:33.200 --> 00:02:37.400
loans. Drop your opinion in the comment

00:02:35.280 --> 00:02:40.680
section. The second major change, the

00:02:37.400 --> 00:02:43.280
CFPB challenges state medical debt

00:02:40.680 --> 00:02:46.520
protections. Now, the CFPB has just

00:02:43.280 --> 00:02:49.080
taken a stand that can lead to major

00:02:46.520 --> 00:02:52.360
court battles when it comes to states

00:02:49.080 --> 00:02:55.160
who have implemented medical debt

00:02:52.360 --> 00:02:57.920
protections for their residents. States

00:02:55.160 --> 00:03:01.080
like California, New York, and Maryland,

00:02:57.920 --> 00:03:04.360
and many others that has put a limit on

00:03:01.080 --> 00:03:07.160
medical debt collections and reporting

00:03:04.360 --> 00:03:09.320
of medical debts to credit reports. With

00:03:07.160 --> 00:03:11.080
these protections implemented by the

00:03:09.320 --> 00:03:13.519
state, many

00:03:11.080 --> 00:03:15.480
advocates believe that states should

00:03:13.519 --> 00:03:18.640
have their own governance and

00:03:15.480 --> 00:03:22.320
protections in place and has that legal

00:03:18.640 --> 00:03:25.959
right. But, the CFPB just took a stand

00:03:22.320 --> 00:03:28.959
that the federal level supersedes states

00:03:25.959 --> 00:03:32.400
authority. And now, debt collectors have

00:03:28.959 --> 00:03:35.920
more power to pursue lawsuits against

00:03:32.400 --> 00:03:39.239
states that prohibit them for collecting

00:03:35.920 --> 00:03:42.280
on this medical debt, including adding

00:03:39.239 --> 00:03:44.360
this medical debt on credit reports.

00:03:42.280 --> 00:03:47.120
Now, I want to be clear that these

00:03:44.360 --> 00:03:50.040
protections right now are not removed,

00:03:47.120 --> 00:03:53.320
but moving forward, you can see legal

00:03:50.040 --> 00:03:55.920
battles and pushback on states that try

00:03:53.320 --> 00:03:58.600
to protect their citizens from medical

00:03:55.920 --> 00:04:01.040
debt collecting on their credit reports.

00:03:58.600 --> 00:04:02.400
So, you need to take these four steps

00:04:01.040 --> 00:04:04.680
right [clears throat] now to protect

00:04:02.400 --> 00:04:07.840
yourself. Step number one, if you

00:04:04.680 --> 00:04:11.040
receive a medical debt collection from a

00:04:07.840 --> 00:04:13.959
debt collection company via mail, you

00:04:11.040 --> 00:04:15.880
want to make sure that you read that

00:04:13.959 --> 00:04:18.799
letter because in the language of that

00:04:15.880 --> 00:04:21.480
letter, you have a right to send a debt

00:04:18.799 --> 00:04:24.480
validation letter. This is for

00:04:21.480 --> 00:04:27.200
collectors to prove they have a legal

00:04:24.480 --> 00:04:29.160
right to collect on that debt. And if

00:04:27.200 --> 00:04:31.240
they can't prove they have a legal right

00:04:29.160 --> 00:04:34.040
to collect on that debt, and if you send

00:04:31.240 --> 00:04:37.120
that letter within 30 days, they cannot

00:04:34.040 --> 00:04:40.000
put that debt on your credit report.

00:04:37.120 --> 00:04:42.680
Now, you want to make sure that you send

00:04:40.000 --> 00:04:45.360
your debt validation letter directly to

00:04:42.680 --> 00:04:48.640
the collection company, and you want to

00:04:45.360 --> 00:04:50.840
send it certified mail. Make sure you do

00:04:48.640 --> 00:04:53.000
not sign that letter because these debt

00:04:50.840 --> 00:04:56.120
collection companies will take your

00:04:53.000 --> 00:04:58.760
signature and put it on a contract. So,

00:04:56.120 --> 00:05:02.200
make sure you never sign those letters.

00:04:58.760 --> 00:05:05.280
And even if you miss that window of time

00:05:02.200 --> 00:05:08.280
to validate that debt in that 30 day,

00:05:05.280 --> 00:05:11.160
you can still send a debt validation

00:05:08.280 --> 00:05:13.960
even after and they must honor it to

00:05:11.160 --> 00:05:16.280
show you they have proof of legal right

00:05:13.960 --> 00:05:18.600
to collect on that debt. Additionally,

00:05:16.280 --> 00:05:21.480
when it comes down to medical debt,

00:05:18.600 --> 00:05:24.600
there's laws in place such as the HIPAA

00:05:21.480 --> 00:05:27.560
law that they cannot have your personal

00:05:24.600 --> 00:05:29.480
and private medical information. If

00:05:27.560 --> 00:05:32.520
they're abiding by the HIPAA law, they

00:05:29.480 --> 00:05:34.720
must store this information properly.

00:05:32.520 --> 00:05:36.840
Many of these debt collection companies,

00:05:34.720 --> 00:05:39.600
when you validate that debt, is going to

00:05:36.840 --> 00:05:43.160
send you back a medical bill, and that

00:05:39.600 --> 00:05:46.080
is a violation of the HIPAA law. So, you

00:05:43.160 --> 00:05:48.200
can also take that stand when that

00:05:46.080 --> 00:05:51.120
happens, and many of times, they will

00:05:48.200 --> 00:05:53.280
back off of that debt. Now, if you need

00:05:51.120 --> 00:05:55.040
these debt validation letters, I do have

00:05:53.280 --> 00:05:57.160
them at my website, so you can pick

00:05:55.040 --> 00:05:59.600
those up. I'll leave that link in the

00:05:57.160 --> 00:06:02.520
description of the video below, but make

00:05:59.600 --> 00:06:04.920
sure you do not sign those letters, but

00:06:02.520 --> 00:06:07.280
make sure that you always send a debt

00:06:04.920 --> 00:06:09.640
validation letter, and keep your

00:06:07.280 --> 00:06:12.600
tracking information when you send those

00:06:09.640 --> 00:06:14.800
letters certified mail. Step number two,

00:06:12.600 --> 00:06:17.480
if you receive a medical bill from your

00:06:14.800 --> 00:06:20.800
medical provider, do not ignore it. You

00:06:17.480 --> 00:06:22.800
want to examine every itemized cost, and

00:06:20.800 --> 00:06:26.320
make sure you check with your insurance

00:06:22.800 --> 00:06:28.760
carrier to see if they paid for that

00:06:26.320 --> 00:06:31.080
medical bill, because many of times, you

00:06:28.760 --> 00:06:33.880
can see these medical providers send

00:06:31.080 --> 00:06:36.360
these debts to collections, even though

00:06:33.880 --> 00:06:38.800
that bill was paid by your insurance

00:06:36.360 --> 00:06:42.040
carrier. Make sure you contact your

00:06:38.800 --> 00:06:44.720
insurance carrier to find out if you owe

00:06:42.040 --> 00:06:47.320
a balance at all. Step number three,

00:06:44.720 --> 00:06:49.760
make sure you check with your state to

00:06:47.320 --> 00:06:52.880
see if they have their own individual

00:06:49.760 --> 00:06:55.560
protections under your state laws. Also,

00:06:52.880 --> 00:06:57.840
make sure that those debt collection

00:06:55.560 --> 00:06:59.600
companies don't have any other

00:06:57.840 --> 00:07:02.200
provisions that they might not be

00:06:59.600 --> 00:07:05.480
abiding by in your law. Many of these

00:07:02.200 --> 00:07:07.840
debt collectors is supposed to be bonded

00:07:05.480 --> 00:07:10.240
in many states in order to operate as a

00:07:07.840 --> 00:07:12.880
debt collector. So, make sure that they

00:07:10.240 --> 00:07:15.320
are compliant with your state law, and

00:07:12.880 --> 00:07:17.720
following all the rules and regulations.

00:07:15.320 --> 00:07:20.320
Step number four, make sure you check

00:07:17.720 --> 00:07:22.880
your credit reports regularly. If you

00:07:20.320 --> 00:07:25.120
see a collection, you want to also

00:07:22.880 --> 00:07:27.720
dispute it with the three major credit

00:07:25.120 --> 00:07:30.560
bureaus. Now, with these debt

00:07:27.720 --> 00:07:32.600
collections, the way they report is very

00:07:30.560 --> 00:07:35.200
important, and many of them violate the

00:07:32.600 --> 00:07:37.720
FCRA if they're reporting that

00:07:35.200 --> 00:07:40.080
collection late every month with AC or

00:07:37.720 --> 00:07:42.360
CO. So, you want to dispute that,

00:07:40.080 --> 00:07:45.120
because that's a violation of the Fair

00:07:42.360 --> 00:07:47.080
Credit Reporting Act. Now, with my user

00:07:45.120 --> 00:07:49.240
Greg of my Elite Credit System, he was

00:07:47.080 --> 00:07:51.280
able to remove a collection within 12

00:07:49.240 --> 00:07:53.200
days. So, if you need my help, that link

00:07:51.280 --> 00:07:54.880
is in the description of the video and

00:07:53.200 --> 00:07:57.400
in the pinned comment section.

00:07:54.880 --> 00:07:59.440
Additionally, always save your

00:07:57.400 --> 00:08:02.800
communications with your insurance

00:07:59.440 --> 00:08:05.480
company, medical care providers, and any

00:08:02.800 --> 00:08:07.120
communications from collection companies

00:08:05.480 --> 00:08:10.480
because those are going to be very

00:08:07.120 --> 00:08:13.120
important if they violate any of the

00:08:10.480 --> 00:08:15.560
laws on the federal level and the state

00:08:13.120 --> 00:08:18.080
level. And that documentation could be

00:08:15.560 --> 00:08:19.960
your best friend if you need to file a

00:08:18.080 --> 00:08:21.560
lawsuit against these collection

00:08:19.960 --> 00:08:23.800
companies. So, hopefully this

00:08:21.560 --> 00:08:25.520
information was helpful. If you have any

00:08:23.800 --> 00:08:27.640
questions or comments, leave it in the

00:08:25.520 --> 00:08:30.040
comment section. More detailed questions

00:08:27.640 --> 00:08:31.880
for me, you can go to my website and all

00:08:30.040 --> 00:08:33.919
your questions go directly to my cell

00:08:31.880 --> 00:08:37.599
phone. I hope to see you guys in the

